-- title:
--   Uniformised locus cut out by an open subset of M
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O$ with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and $(r)=(\pi)$, together with a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal and every element satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ whose value at that element lies in that ideal. Let $G$ be a type, and let $f_M : M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be a morphism of schemes that is locally of finite type. Write $F$ for the functor on $\mathcal O$-algebras sending $B$ to $((O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}_{K_0,\pi}(B)) \times G$, where a Deligne datum assigns to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ with invertible quotient, compatibly with inclusions and homotheties and subject to the nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $B$; and write $F_M$ for the functor sending $B$ to the set of sections $\operatorname{Spec} B \to M$ of $f_M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Assume given maps $\Theta_B : F(B) \to F_M(B)$, for all $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, that are natural in $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms between such $B$, and formally étale in the following sense: for every surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $p : B \to B_0$ between such algebras whose kernel has pairwise zero products, every $x_0 \in F(B_0)$ and every $y \in F_M(B)$ with $p_*y = \Theta_{B_0}(x_0)$, there is a unique $x \in F(B)$ with $p_*x = x_0$ and $\Theta_B(x) = y$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an open subset $V$ of the underlying space of $M$ such that for every point $x$ of $M$: $x$ lies in $V$ and is the image of the closed point under some $y \in F_M(k)$ for some algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, if and only if there are such $k$ and $y$ with $x$ the image of the closed point and moreover $y = \Theta_k((\psi,P),g)$ for some $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$, some Deligne datum $P$ over $k$ and some $g \in G$.
--
--   This is the openness statement underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the locus of geometric $\pi$-nilpotent points of $M$ that come from the formal upper half plane datum together with the label set $G$ is the trace on such points of an open subset of $M$. It is stated for an arbitrary target $M$ locally of finite type over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ carrying a natural formally étale family $\Theta$, so that each level of the Hecke tower may invoke it with its own $(M, f_M, \Theta)$; it is used in the identification of the uniformised locus inside a fine moduli scheme of quaternionic type.
